This file lists the third-party JavaScript/font assets the webmail UI
vendors into `mailosh/web/static/vendor/`, `.../icons/`, `.../fonts/`
(fetched/built by `make vendor icons fonts`, pinned in the top-level
Makefile). Those files are gitignored — not committed to this repository —
but they ARE copied into the built Docker image (see
`docker/mailosh.Dockerfile`), so this is a record of what's actually
distributed, not just what's in source control. Versions/licenses below
were verified directly against each package's own published metadata and
LICENSE file on the date noted per entry.

Two of the entries below — Squire and DOMPurify — are vendored and shipped
in the image but are not yet loaded by any page: both belong to the compose
editor (Phase 1C), which has not landed. Squire is the editor itself and
DOMPurify sanitises what a user pastes into it, in the browser. Neither has
anything to do with reading mail: the Phase 1B sanitiser that renders an
incoming message is entirely server-side Python — `nh3` (the Rust `ammonia`
binding) for tags, attributes and URL policy, `tinycss2` for CSS — and it
loads no JavaScript library at all. They are listed anyway, because the
image distributes them and this file records what is distributed.

Re-verified 2026-09-03: every file in `mailosh/web/static/vendor/`, plus
`static/fonts/InterVariable.woff2`, is byte-for-byte identical to the pinned
upstream URL in the Makefile (sha256 compared directly), and
`command-score.js` is byte-for-byte the pinned upstream commit with only the
one documented export-line rewrite applied. Every version and license below
was re-checked against upstream package metadata and LICENSE files on the
same date; nothing needed correcting.

