* Alpine.js 3.17.1 — the **CSP build**, `@alpinejs/csp`, vendored as
  `vendor/alpine.min.js`
  https://alpinejs.dev/advanced/csp
  (https://github.com/alpinejs/alpine, `packages/csp`)
  License: MIT (from the package's own published metadata, checked
  directly against registry.npmjs.org, 2026-09-02)
  Build: this is deliberately NOT the standard `alpinejs` distribution.
  The webmail serves `script-src 'self'` with no `'unsafe-eval'`, and the
  standard build evaluates every template expression through
  `new AsyncFunction` — which fails at *runtime*, the first time a
  directive is evaluated, not at build time. The CSP build ships its own
  parser instead of that constructor, and contains no
  `Function`/`AsyncFunction` constructor call at all — verified directly
  against the vendored bytes. That parser accepts a real expression
  grammar (property paths, computed access, method calls with arguments,
  ternaries, arithmetic, comparison, object/array literals) and rejects
  template literals, out-of-scope globals, multi-statement expressions,
  spread/destructuring and inline function definitions.
  Pin: exact version, replacing the floating `alpinejs@3` this previously
  carried, so a new upstream 3.x cannot change what ships without this
  file and the Makefile being touched — the same discipline the
  command-score and Inter entries below/above already record.

